# No .env file is needed for the native iPad app.
# Never put device access tokens or provider credentials in EXPO_PUBLIC variables.
# The HTTPS API origin is prefilled. Use OS-authenticated Host → Private setup
# to consume the owner's one-time QR/code; the scoped booth credential is stored
# in this device's Keychain with SecureStore. Guests never enter tokens.
# Development builds can test an HTTP loopback API, e.g. http://localhost:8787.
# Loopback readiness never produces a guest QR. A physical booth needs a reachable
# public HTTPS origin; localhost means the iPad itself.
